WEBVTT

00:02.509 --> 00:03.635
KATARA: Water...

00:04.844 --> 00:06.596
Earth...

00:06.721 --> 00:08.723
Fire...

00:08.848 --> 00:11.267
Air.

00:11.351 --> 00:12.519
Long ago...

00:12.602 --> 00:15.355
The four nations lived
together in harmony.

00:15.438 --> 00:19.234
Then everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

00:19.317 --> 00:23.696
Only the Avatar master of
all four elements could stop them.

00:23.780 --> 00:25.490
But when the world
needed him most

00:25.573 --> 00:27.367
he vanished.

00:27.450 --> 00:31.037
100 years passed, and my brother
and I discovered the new Avatar

00:31.120 --> 00:32.956
an airbender named Aang.

00:33.039 --> 00:35.166
And although his airbending
skills were great

00:35.250 --> 00:37.794
he has a lot to learn before
he's ready to save anyone.

00:37.877 --> 00:38.962
AANG: Oof.

00:39.045 --> 00:42.507
But I believe Aang
can save the world.

00:42.590 --> 00:44.592
( ♪... )

00:47.929 --> 00:50.807
( MAN READING )

00:50.932 --> 00:52.892
AANG: Blending in is better
than hiding out.

00:53.017 --> 00:54.852
If we get Fire Nation disguises,

00:54.936 --> 00:57.647
we'll be just as safe as we would be
hiding in a cave.

00:57.730 --> 00:59.983
You have no right
to judge me, Uncle.

01:00.066 --> 01:04.237
I did what I had to do in Ba Sing Se,
and you were a fool for not joining me.

01:07.282 --> 01:10.076
I see you favor
the White Lotus Gambit.

01:10.159 --> 01:12.579
Not many still cling
to the ancient ways.

01:13.580 --> 01:16.791
Those who do can always
find a friend.

01:26.050 --> 01:29.637
KATARA: Wow, this is amazing
to watch.

01:29.762 --> 01:32.515
Kind of makes you realize
how insignificant we are.

01:32.640 --> 01:36.728
Eh, you've seen nothing once,
you've seen it 1,000 times.

01:36.811 --> 01:38.396
( ALL GASPING )

01:38.521 --> 01:39.731
SOKKA: Oh, man.

01:39.856 --> 01:41.566
You've never not seen
anything like this.

01:47.113 --> 01:48.364
( EXPLOSION )

01:57.206 --> 01:59.584
KATARA: The fire is gonna
destroy that town.

01:59.667 --> 02:01.044
AANG: Not if we can stop it.

02:01.544 --> 02:03.880
( GROWLING )

02:04.255 --> 02:05.590
There's a creek over here.

02:05.673 --> 02:07.425
I'll bend the water
on to the fire.

02:07.508 --> 02:10.303
Toph, let's make a trench
to keep the fire from coming any closer.

02:12.138 --> 02:13.181
What should I do?

02:13.306 --> 02:14.307
( MOMO SQUAWKING )

02:14.432 --> 02:15.933
Keep an eye on Momo.

02:16.726 --> 02:19.479
So what, I'm just
a lemur-sitter?

02:19.562 --> 02:20.563
There, there.

02:20.647 --> 02:21.648
Feel better?

02:30.281 --> 02:35.161
( GASPING )

02:58.434 --> 03:00.978
Sokka, stand clear.

03:01.062 --> 03:02.897
Right, stand clear.

03:02.980 --> 03:04.148
Got it.

03:04.232 --> 03:05.733
( INHALING )

03:07.485 --> 03:09.612
( GASPING )

03:13.741 --> 03:16.035
Good work, everybody.

03:18.204 --> 03:20.456
( MOMO WARBLING )

03:32.218 --> 03:33.302
( GASPING )

03:33.386 --> 03:34.679
( MAKING EATING NOISES )

03:34.762 --> 03:36.097
MAN: Look at you.

03:36.180 --> 03:38.766
You're just a fat,
disgusting old man.

03:39.350 --> 03:40.768
You do nothing, you say nothing.

03:40.893 --> 03:44.397
You just eat and roll around
in your own filth like a pig.

03:45.189 --> 03:46.357
You're a disgrace.

04:01.831 --> 04:05.501
These people have no idea how close
they were to getting toasted last night.

04:05.626 --> 04:08.504
Yeah, the worst thing
about being in disguise

04:08.588 --> 04:10.214
is we don't get
the hero worship anymore.

04:10.339 --> 04:12.091
I miss the love.

04:12.216 --> 04:14.969
Boo-hoo, poor heroes.

04:15.595 --> 04:16.971
What's your problem?

04:17.054 --> 04:19.265
You haven't even touched
your smoked sea slug.

04:19.348 --> 04:22.393
It's just, all you guys can do
this awesome bending stuff

04:22.477 --> 04:27.023
like putting out forest fires, and flying
around, and making other stuff fly around.

04:27.732 --> 04:29.484
I can't fly around, OK?

04:29.776 --> 04:32.153
I can't do anything.

04:32.487 --> 04:33.488
That's not true.

04:33.613 --> 04:35.948
No one can read a map like you.

04:36.032 --> 04:37.742
I can't read at all.

04:37.867 --> 04:40.495
Yeah, and who keeps us laughing
with sarcastic comments all the time?

04:40.620 --> 04:43.456
I mean,
look at Katara's hair, right?

04:43.581 --> 04:45.500
- What's up with that?
- What?

04:45.625 --> 04:46.918
What's wrong with my hair?

04:47.043 --> 04:48.920
Nothing, I was just trying to...

04:49.045 --> 04:51.964
SOKKA: Look, I appreciate
the effort, but the fact is

04:52.089 --> 04:56.803
each of you is so amazing
and so special, and I'm not.

04:58.387 --> 05:00.681
I'm just the guy
in the group who's regular.

05:04.018 --> 05:05.561
I'm sorry you're feeling so down,

05:05.645 --> 05:08.189
but I hope you know none of us
see you that way.

05:10.900 --> 05:13.152
I know something that's gonna
make you feel better.

05:13.236 --> 05:14.737
You do?

05:14.821 --> 05:16.781
Shopping.

05:17.824 --> 05:21.369
Maybe a little something
to reinvigorate my battling.

05:21.452 --> 05:22.578
Hey, how about these?

05:23.746 --> 05:24.872
Hi-ya!

05:24.997 --> 05:26.290
"Smack-a-dacka-doo!"

05:26.415 --> 05:30.294
( GRUNTING )

05:30.837 --> 05:32.255
AANG: What do you think?

05:34.215 --> 05:36.217
Pretty slick, huh?

05:36.342 --> 05:38.386
All I need to complete
the outfit is a wind sword.

05:38.511 --> 05:39.762
What's a wind sword?

05:39.887 --> 05:41.681
It's where I get a sword handle

05:41.806 --> 05:44.559
And then I just swing
this around and bend air out like a blade.

05:44.684 --> 05:47.728
( MAKING WHOOSHING SOUND )

05:47.854 --> 05:50.106
Yeah, nice.

05:50.231 --> 05:52.733
( WHIMPERING )

05:52.859 --> 05:54.360
I'll just stick to what I got.

05:59.574 --> 06:03.160
( GROANING )

06:03.286 --> 06:04.328
( GRUNTING )

06:19.343 --> 06:21.095
Ooh.

06:22.054 --> 06:24.181
That's what Sokka's
talking about.

06:24.265 --> 06:25.349
MAN: You have a good eye.

06:25.433 --> 06:27.226
That's an original from Piandao

06:27.310 --> 06:30.229
the greatest sword master
and sword maker in Fire Nation history.

06:30.354 --> 06:32.940
He lives in the big castle
up the road from here.

06:33.941 --> 06:35.401
That's it.

06:35.484 --> 06:36.986
That's what you needed
all along, Sokka.

06:37.069 --> 06:38.070
A sword?

06:38.154 --> 06:39.238
Not the sword.

06:39.322 --> 06:40.823
A master.

06:40.907 --> 06:42.950
We've all had masters
to help us get better.

06:43.117 --> 06:44.994
You should see if you
can study with Piandao.

06:45.077 --> 06:46.287
That's a great idea.

06:46.370 --> 06:49.165
I could've never gotten to where
I am without Master Pakku.

06:49.248 --> 06:50.750
Everyone needs a teacher.

06:51.334 --> 06:53.085
I learned from badger moles.

06:53.169 --> 06:55.171
They don't talk,
but they're still good teachers.

06:56.255 --> 06:59.216
It would be nice to be
a master swordfighter.

07:00.217 --> 07:01.802
All right, I'll talk to him.

07:09.435 --> 07:13.105
( GRUNTING )

07:26.452 --> 07:27.536
( GASPING )

07:27.620 --> 07:28.955
Can I help you?

07:30.831 --> 07:32.375
I've come to train
with the master.

07:32.583 --> 07:36.253
You should know the master
turns almost everyone away.

07:36.337 --> 07:38.172
What did you bring him
to prove your worth?

07:39.215 --> 07:41.717
Well, uh...

07:41.801 --> 07:43.177
Right.

07:43.260 --> 07:44.887
Let's get this over with.

07:55.898 --> 07:57.900
Master, my name is Sokka,

07:57.984 --> 08:00.319
and I wish to be instructed
in the way of the sword.

08:00.403 --> 08:01.612
PIANDAO: Sokka.

08:01.737 --> 08:03.406
That's an unusual name.

08:03.531 --> 08:05.032
Oh, uh, really?

08:05.157 --> 08:07.326
Uh, where I come from,
the Fire Nation colonies

08:07.410 --> 08:11.163
it's a pretty normal name,
for Fire Nation colonials.

08:11.247 --> 08:12.915
PIANDAO: Let me guess.

08:13.040 --> 08:15.543
You've come hundreds of miles
from your little village

08:15.668 --> 08:18.462
where you're the best
swordsman in town

08:18.546 --> 08:21.674
and you think you deserve
to learn from the master.

08:21.799 --> 08:24.260
Well, actually, I've been
all over the world.

08:24.593 --> 08:26.887
PIANDAO: Yep, here we go.

08:26.971 --> 08:30.933
And I know one thing for sure,
I have a lot to learn.

08:31.851 --> 08:34.979
You're not doing a very good job
of selling yourself.

08:35.062 --> 08:36.564
I know.

08:36.647 --> 08:39.483
Your butler told me that when I met you,
I would have to prove my worth

08:39.567 --> 08:42.361
But the truth is,
I don't know if I am worthy.

08:42.445 --> 08:44.739
Hm, I see.

08:45.698 --> 08:50.494
Well, then, let's find out
together how worthy you are.

08:52.580 --> 08:54.373
I will train you.

09:00.463 --> 09:04.800
The first thing you must learn is that
your weapon is an extension of yourself.

09:04.884 --> 09:08.137
You must think of it as
another part of your own body.

09:10.014 --> 09:11.390
Like a second head.

09:11.766 --> 09:16.520
Well, more like
an extra-long, really sharp arm.

09:16.604 --> 09:20.566
The sword is a simple tool,
but in the hands of a master

09:20.649 --> 09:26.363
it becomes the most versatile of weapons,
and just as the imagination is limitless

09:26.447 --> 09:29.700
so too are the possibilities
of the sword.

09:32.369 --> 09:33.704
AANG: What should we do today?

09:33.788 --> 09:34.997
I'm tapped out.

09:35.081 --> 09:36.999
I already picked my toes, twice.

09:37.083 --> 09:38.584
Twice?

09:38.667 --> 09:40.044
The first time was for cleaning,

09:40.127 --> 09:43.547
but the second time's just for
the sweet picking sensation.

09:44.090 --> 09:45.674
Sokka's been in charge
of the schedule.

09:45.758 --> 09:47.676
I'm not sure
what we should be doing.

09:47.760 --> 09:50.930
Plus, it's so hot today.

09:51.013 --> 09:52.306
How hot is it?

09:52.389 --> 09:53.390
I don't know.

09:53.474 --> 09:54.725
Real hot?

09:54.850 --> 10:00.898
It's so hot, it's so hot,
Momo is shedding like Appa.

10:00.981 --> 10:04.568
Huh, huh?

10:05.569 --> 10:07.571
I guess the jokes
don't run in the family.

10:07.863 --> 10:09.865
KATARA: Oh, everyone's a critic.

10:09.949 --> 10:11.408
( APPA GROWLING )

10:11.492 --> 10:13.869
( GRUNTING )

10:21.627 --> 10:26.841
The warrior practices a variety
of arts to keep his mind sharp and fluid.

10:26.924 --> 10:29.760
The first you will learn
is calligraphy.

10:29.844 --> 10:31.428
Write your name.

10:31.929 --> 10:34.473
Writing my name will make me
a better swordsman?

10:34.598 --> 10:38.853
When you write your name,
you stamp the paper with your identity.

10:38.936 --> 10:43.232
You must learn to use your sword
to stamp your identity on a battlefield.

10:47.361 --> 10:53.200
Remember, you cannot take back a stroke of
the brush, or a stroke of the sword.

10:57.329 --> 10:59.498
You are getting ink
on your face.

10:59.582 --> 11:01.041
I am?

11:01.125 --> 11:02.376
I am.

11:02.501 --> 11:04.837
So this is about putting
my identity on the page, right?

11:21.979 --> 11:27.610
( GRUNTING )

11:30.487 --> 11:34.950
Landscape painting teaches a warrior
to hold the lay of the land in his mind.

11:36.160 --> 11:38.495
( GRUNTING )

11:38.579 --> 11:41.957
In battle, you only have an instant
to take everything in.

11:50.007 --> 11:52.635
Now, paint it.

11:53.761 --> 11:54.887
And no peeking.

12:09.693 --> 12:12.071
SOKKA: I'm finished.

12:14.031 --> 12:15.616
You added a rainbow.

12:16.825 --> 12:18.452
Is that OK?

12:18.577 --> 12:20.537
( SIGHING )

12:23.499 --> 12:25.251
( GRUNTING )

12:25.376 --> 12:27.294
PIANDAO: Sokka.

12:27.419 --> 12:29.213
( GRUNTING )

12:29.338 --> 12:31.465
Concentrate on
what you're doing.

12:33.300 --> 12:36.887
Rock gardening teaches the warrior
to manipulate his surroundings

12:37.012 --> 12:39.515
and use them to his advantage.

12:40.057 --> 12:43.936
Hm, manipulate them
to my advantage.

12:44.019 --> 12:45.187
Oh.

12:47.564 --> 12:49.900
( GRUNTING )

13:00.661 --> 13:03.205
Ah.

13:04.581 --> 13:06.292
( GASPING )

13:06.375 --> 13:08.585
Hey, would you mind grabbing
a cold drink for me?

13:08.752 --> 13:09.753
( GASPING )

13:09.837 --> 13:11.755
I'll take a slice of lemon
in mine, please.

13:11.839 --> 13:13.090
( SIGHING )

13:50.711 --> 13:52.171
What's going on in there?

13:57.843 --> 13:59.053
Crazy old man.

14:05.809 --> 14:07.603
KATARA: So where are
we going next?

14:08.103 --> 14:09.730
We're starting from here.

14:09.813 --> 14:11.565
No, we're over on this island.

14:11.982 --> 14:14.735
You noodle-brains don't know
what you're doing.

14:14.860 --> 14:16.612
I miss Sokka.

14:16.695 --> 14:18.489
Ooh, I got one.

14:18.614 --> 14:22.242
If you miss him so much,
why don't you marry him?

14:29.750 --> 14:31.835
PIANDAO: You've had a good
first day of training.

14:31.919 --> 14:33.504
I have?

14:33.629 --> 14:35.964
But I thought I messed up
every single thing we worked on.

14:36.048 --> 14:39.301
You messed things up
in a very special way.

14:39.426 --> 14:42.096
You are ready for a real sword.

14:42.179 --> 14:43.180
( GASPING )

14:43.263 --> 14:44.306
Are you giving me one of yours?

14:44.431 --> 14:45.432
No.

14:45.516 --> 14:46.600
( GROANING )

14:46.725 --> 14:49.853
Your sword must be
an extension of yourself

14:49.978 --> 14:53.899
So tomorrow, you will make
your own sword.

15:02.199 --> 15:06.703
Choosing the correct material is the
most important step in crafting a sword.

15:06.787 --> 15:09.164
You must trust your steel
with your life.

15:09.248 --> 15:10.249
Choose carefully.

15:13.377 --> 15:15.671
( GRUNTING )

15:17.339 --> 15:19.174
Master, would it be possible for me to

15:19.258 --> 15:22.010
leave and bring back
a special material for my sword?

15:22.094 --> 15:24.346
I wouldn't have it
any other way.

15:27.641 --> 15:29.601
- Sokka's coming.
-( GASPING )

15:29.685 --> 15:31.145
Hey, guys.
What are you doing?

15:31.228 --> 15:32.646
AANG: Sokka?
TOPH: You're back.

15:32.729 --> 15:34.440
We missed you so much.

15:34.940 --> 15:36.358
Say something funny.

15:36.442 --> 15:37.901
Funny how?

15:37.985 --> 15:40.154
( LAUGHING )

15:40.779 --> 15:41.989
What's their deal?

15:42.114 --> 15:43.323
I don't know.

15:43.449 --> 15:45.075
They missed you or something.

15:45.159 --> 15:46.743
I didn't care.

15:46.827 --> 15:49.204
Thanks.
That warms my heart.

15:49.329 --> 15:50.706
Anyway, I need some help.

16:05.679 --> 16:07.890
( BREATHING HEAVILY )

16:26.825 --> 16:27.868
Who's this?

16:27.951 --> 16:29.786
Oh, these are my friends.

16:29.870 --> 16:31.872
Just other good
Fire Nation folks.

16:33.081 --> 16:35.751
Do you think we can make
a sword out of a meteorite?

16:36.543 --> 16:40.172
We'll make a sword unlike
any other in the world.

17:38.230 --> 17:42.401
Sokka, when you first arrived,
you were so unsure.

17:42.484 --> 17:45.195
You even seemed
down on yourself.

17:45.279 --> 17:47.864
But I saw something
in you right away.

17:47.990 --> 17:52.661
I saw a heart as strong as
a lion turtle, and twice as big

17:52.744 --> 17:56.999
and as we trained, it wasn't
your skills that impressed me.

17:57.082 --> 18:00.711
No, it certainly
wasn't your skills.

18:01.962 --> 18:05.132
You showed something
beyond that.

18:05.841 --> 18:10.095
Creativity, versatility,
intelligence.

18:10.178 --> 18:13.599
These are the traits
that define a great swordsman

18:13.682 --> 18:17.436
and these are the traits
that define you.

18:17.519 --> 18:21.732
You told me you didn't know
if you were worthy

18:21.857 --> 18:27.738
but I believe that you are more worthy
than any man I have ever trained.

18:30.782 --> 18:32.367
I'm sorry, master.

18:32.451 --> 18:33.493
You're wrong.

18:33.619 --> 18:35.829
I am not worthy.

18:36.038 --> 18:37.664
I'm not who you think I am.

18:37.789 --> 18:38.874
I'm not from the Fire Nation.

18:38.999 --> 18:41.293
I'm from the Southern
Water Tribe.

18:41.376 --> 18:44.046
I lied so that I could
learn swordsmanship from you.

18:44.880 --> 18:45.964
I'm sorry.

18:47.257 --> 18:49.426
I'm sorry, too.

18:49.509 --> 18:51.219
( GASPING )

18:52.596 --> 18:56.642
No, this is my fight, alone.

19:00.604 --> 19:03.357
You used to be
the pride of the Fire Nation.

19:03.482 --> 19:06.234
Our top general,
The Dragon of the West.

19:06.360 --> 19:10.072
Now, look at you.

19:10.822 --> 19:12.115
Look what you've become.

19:23.835 --> 19:24.920
( GRUNTING )

19:48.735 --> 19:51.822
( GRUNTING )

20:05.377 --> 20:07.212
PIANDAO: Excellent.

20:07.295 --> 20:09.297
Using your superior agility
against an older opponent.

20:09.423 --> 20:10.632
Smart.

20:15.595 --> 20:17.305
( GRUNTING )

20:27.774 --> 20:29.151
PIANDAO: Good use of terrain.

20:29.234 --> 20:30.402
Fighting from the high ground.

20:35.866 --> 20:37.159
( GRUNTING )

20:56.052 --> 20:58.638
Yes, use your surroundings.

20:58.764 --> 21:00.515
Make them fight for you.

21:01.892 --> 21:03.393
( SCREAMING )

21:03.477 --> 21:05.437
( PANTING )

21:10.692 --> 21:11.735
( GRUNTING )

21:15.113 --> 21:16.573
( COUGHING )

21:17.783 --> 21:19.743
Very resourceful.

21:48.480 --> 21:50.023
Excellent work, Sokka.

21:58.198 --> 22:01.576
I think I'm a little old
to be fighting the Avatar.

22:03.161 --> 22:04.454
How did you know?

22:04.621 --> 22:06.289
Oh, I've been around a while.

22:06.414 --> 22:08.166
You pick things up.

22:08.291 --> 22:10.836
Of course, I knew from the beginning
that Sokka was Water Tribe.

22:11.670 --> 22:15.215
You might want to think of
a better Fire Nation cover name.

22:15.298 --> 22:16.508
Try "Lee."

22:16.633 --> 22:18.760
There's a million Lees.

22:18.844 --> 22:22.013
But why would you agree
to train someone from the water tribe?

22:22.097 --> 22:25.225
The way of the sword doesn't
belong to any one nation.

22:25.308 --> 22:28.061
Knowledge of the arts
belongs to us all.

22:31.439 --> 22:36.778
Sokka, you must continue
your training on your own.

22:36.945 --> 22:40.740
If you stay on this path,
I know that one day

22:40.824 --> 22:43.827
you will become an even
greater master than I am.

22:52.586 --> 22:54.588
Wait.

22:55.130 --> 22:59.634
The master wanted you to have this,
as something to remember him by.

23:06.391 --> 23:07.934
It's a Pai Sho tile.

23:08.018 --> 23:09.936
AANG: The White Lotus.
Hm.

23:10.020 --> 23:11.313
KATARA: What does it mean?

23:11.396 --> 23:12.856
I have no idea.

23:16.234 --> 23:17.861
Ooh, that reminds me.

23:17.944 --> 23:19.487
Toph, I thought
you might like this

23:19.571 --> 23:22.240
Since you've probably never had a chance
to bend space earth before.

23:23.074 --> 23:24.242
Sweet.

23:26.411 --> 23:27.704
Check this out.

23:30.373 --> 23:32.751
You know, I don't think there's
such a thing as "space earth."

23:32.834 --> 23:35.712
If it's from space,
